          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What does guidance describe as initial management for reflux before any investigation?",
          "answer": "For adults experiencing typical symptoms of heartburn and regurgitation, and without any \"alarm features\" (which would prompt further investigation), guidelines suggest an initial approach of an eight-week trial of acid suppression. This involves taking a proton pump inhibitor before a meal. This empiric treatment is recommended before any investigations are undertaken (Gastroenterology society clinical guideline).\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
